<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cretan Koinon</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cretan Koinon was a federation of the city-states of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a> formed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellenistic-period">Hellenistic period</a> and attested from the late third century BCE. It provided a common assembly and a court for disputes between cities, though rivalries, especially between Knossos and Gortyn, often divided it, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-v-of-macedon">Philip V of Macedon</a> became its protector around 216 BCE. Revived under Roman rule, it later administered the imperial cult on the island.</p></div>
